It is early afternoon and very warm.
I am still walking across the flea market.
But suddenly the sky turns dark.
A strong summer rain begins.
Immediately, the vendors react.
They quickly throw plastic sheets over their tables.
I quickly run to a large tree.
There I stand in the dry.
I hold the backpack close to my body.
I look into the rain and think.
Three months ago, I was also standing in the rain.
Back then it was freezing and unpleasant.
But this rain today is completely different from the rain in March.
This summer rain is warm.
The air immediately smells fresh and good.
Nevertheless, the rain is getting heavier and heavier.
The tree does not offer enough protection.
I need a better place.
